{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>My offering, my food for the fire.</b> The section of offerings was juxtaposed here because Moses had already been commanded to warn Israel concerning the offerings that they are obligated to perform. And now, when he saw that he would not enter the land with them, he made known to them the matter of the offerings, and he began with the offering of the daily burnt-offering, even though he had already mentioned it in the section of ואתה תצוה — and there it was a warning for the days of ordination." "<b>And by way of</b> the plain sense (peshat): קרבני — this is the blood; את — to include salt, as it is written (Leviticus 2): ״על כל קרבנך תקריב מלח״ — therefore they dip the bread of the מוציא in salt, because the offering is called 'bread' (לחם); לחמי — these are the portions offered by fire (אמורין); לאשי — those given to the fire upon my altar; תשמרו — that there be priests, Levites, and Israelites standing watch over it; from here they learned and instituted the מעמדות (ma'amadot); במועדו — that is, each and every day is the appointed time of the daily offerings; but it also comes to say that nothing should precede the morning burnt-offering and nothing should follow after the evening burnt-offering; במועדו — even on the Sabbath and even in a state of impurity."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:36:38.761434231Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}